# Workspace Conventions

## Branch Structure

This workspace contains three directories. They are NOT interchangeable:

- **meshcore-open-unified/** — The active working branch with the most changes. ALL feature development and improvements happen here. This is the only directory you should be editing.
- **meshcore-open-pr173/** (and similar pr directories) — Small, single-feature branches created from unified for submitting PRs. Each PR branch isolates one feature for review.
- **meshcore-open/** — The PUBLIC upstream repository. DO NOT TOUCH. This is only updated when PRs are merged upstream. Never edit, commit, or modify anything in this directory.

## Git Push Default

- In this workspace, when the user asks to "push" without a target branch, default to pushing to `feature/unified-all-changes` on `origin`.
- Ask before pushing if the local branch is not `feature/unified-all-changes` or if pushing would require a force push.

## Commit Discipline

- Commit after every successful build. If flutter build apk --debug succeeds, commit immediately before moving on.
- Commit before starting a new feature. The working tree should be clean when beginning new work.
- Never leave broken code uncommitted overnight. If something does not compile, either fix it or stash it.
- Use descriptive commit messages that name the feature or fix, not "WIP" or "updates".

## Build and Deploy

- Always build and test on the meshcore-open-unified/ directory.
- For phone updates, use in-place install only: `adb install -r <apk>`.
- Never use `flutter install` in this workspace because it may uninstall first and wipe app data.
- If install fails with `INSTALL_FAILED_UPDATE_INCOMPATIBLE`, stop and ask before any uninstall action.
- Verify dart analyze lib/ passes with zero errors before committing.

## Feature Work

- Develop features directly in meshcore-open-unified/.
- When a feature is complete and tested, create a separate PR branch (meshcore-open-prNNN/) with just that feature changes isolated.
- Do NOT refactor or restructure code unrelated to the current task.
- Keep changes minimal and focused on the requested feature.
